1
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,480
Morning!

2
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:24,240
Is that for Elsa?

3
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:26,120
Yes.

4
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:27,880
You locked her up last night.

5
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:29,960
She must be furious.

6
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:32,520
You love Elsa very much,

7
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:35,840
why must it come to this?

8
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:38,320
Because she's getting out of hand.

9
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:40,880
Just like her sister.

10
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:43,960
Elsa has always been a good kid.

11
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:48,680
Looks like she must really love this guy.

12
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:51,200
They just started dating.

13
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:53,360
How much in love can she be?

14
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:55,600
If we force them apart,

15
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:57,600
what if she'll end up like Emma?

16
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:01,280
Locking her up will not work.

17
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:03,520
What else can we do?

18
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:06,960
We're leaving tomorrow night.

19
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:10,640
After we settle down over there,

20
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,880
we'll have a long talk with her.

21
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:17,360
What will happen over there?

22
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:21,000
What else? We'll start over.

23
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:24,840
You're doing so well here
and you have a good job.

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
You're giving up everything for me.

25
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,880
What do you mean? We're family.

26
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:33,280
I won't be separated from you.

27
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,200
Why don't you stay?

28
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:37,440
Elsa and I will go back, OK?

29
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:39,680
You think I'll let that happen?

30
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:42,000
What if you run into that creep?

31
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:43,840
That's too dangerous.

32
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,920
I have no appetite. I'm not eating.

33
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,280
I'll head back to work.

34
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:50,720
Don't get any ideas.

35
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:03,280
You're awake. Want some breakfast?

36
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:07,840
Now I know why Emma had to leave.

37
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:11,000
We have the same fate.

38
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:13,920
Daddy won't let me out either.

39
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,720
You'll be free in two days.

40
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:20,480
Free? I can't even have friends.

41
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:23,200
You asked me all those questions that night,

42
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:25,720
because you're in love with this guy?

43
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,440
His name is YY.

44
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:33,280
We became friends because
he helped me look for Emma.

45
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:35,600
He's smart and is good to me

46
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:37,040
and is always thinking for me.

47
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:39,920
Just like when I found something about Emma

48
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,560
and wanted to call the Police.

49
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:42,640
He stopped me

50
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,880
because he didn't want the Police
to know about me.

51
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:47,400
If he wanted to hurt me,

52
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,960
why would he do that?

53
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:50,720
But Daddy won't believe him

54
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:52,560
and insisted YY was up to no good.

55
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,560
Daddy has his reasons.

56
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:57,600
Mom, can you let me out?

57
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:00,880
You met YY at the wrong time.

58
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:03,280
Wait till we settle down abroad

59
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:05,280
and you have proper proof of identity,

60
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:07,280
he can join us there.

61
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:10,240
Wait? How long must I wait?

62
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,800
I only want to see him one last time.

63
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:16,840
Now I know loving someone can be so hard.

64
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:21,440
I don't want to leave and be away from YY.

65
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:25,200
I'll do my best to protect you.

66
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:28,640
Are you willing to spend
the rest of your life with me

67
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,960
and build a family?

68
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:42,320
Just be patient.

69
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:45,960
If he's your Mr. Right like your Daddy,

70
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:48,320
you two will always be together.

71
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:53,280
The number you called
cannot be connected now.

72
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,080
She won't pick up or return my messages.

73
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,800
Please be OK.

74
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:02,240
Excuse me, have you seen this girl?

75
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:13,600
Excuse me, have you seen her?

76
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:17,960
Sorry...have you seen this girl?

77
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,120
No!

78
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,200
Thanks.

79
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:39,520
Excuse me, have you seen her, Uncle?

80
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:42,720
Young man, you already asked me
this morning.

81
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:45,200
Sorry!

82
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:48,320
I'm finished with lunch,

83
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:50,160
you're still looking for her?

84
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,960
You love her that much?

85
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:56,480
I'm worried.

86
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:58,640
Didn't hear from her all night.

87
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,160
I'm afraid something happened to her.

88
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:01,680
Don't be silly.

89
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:05,120
She wants to ditch you.
That's why she's ghosting you.

90
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:07,640
You expect one month's notice?

91
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:10,640
There are other trees in the forest.

92
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:12,960
Find someone else.

93
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:16,880
Don't torture yourself over one girl.

94
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:20,520
She's not the type to give up easily.

95
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:26,720
However hard it is, I want to be with her.

96
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:31,280
YY, I promised you

97
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:33,200
we'll meet again before I leave.

98
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,600
But I guess by the time you get this letter,

99
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:38,240
I should have left. Sorry!

100
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:41,920
Once I settle down, I'll be in touch.

101
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:44,720
We'll meet again if it's in our destiny.

102
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,520
What are you doing?

103
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:09,600
Writing a letter to YY.

104
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:11,080
Since you won't let me out,

105
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:13,280
I must find a way to say goodbye.

106
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:18,680
Mom, promise me you'll make sure
he gets this.

107
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:22,480
He'll be worried if he didn't hear from me.

108
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,160
Please, Mom?

109
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:26,480
I'm not sending this to him.

110
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:30,200
Here...
What do you mean?

111
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:42,960
You want me to say goodbye on the phone?

112
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:45,680
I want you to tell him in person
you're leaving.

113
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,240
After you settle down, you will contact him.

114
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:49,400
Really?

115
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:52,160
Thanks, Mom!

116
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:56,880
What made you change your mind?

117
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:58,880
I was going to the bank...

118
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:01,200
I saw YY looking everywhere for you.

119
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,800
People told him to give up,

120
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:06,640
but he said he wants to be with you.

121
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:09,200
What a fool!

122
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:11,600
I can tell he loves you very much

123
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,120
and cares a great deal about you.

124
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:15,960
You were right. He'll take good care of you.

125
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:19,040
Mom, I knew you'll like him.

126
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:22,000
I won't separate you by force.

127
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:24,640
Because you have a good relationship.

128
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:26,240
You must treasure it.

129
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,400
I will.

130
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:30,040
OK, go find him.

131
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:32,600
Remember to be home before dark.

132
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:34,560
Today is Daddy's last day.

133
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,320
He should leave early.

134
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:39,600
Alright?

135
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,880
Don't worry! I don't want to leave YY,

136
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:45,600
I also don't want to leave you and Daddy.

137
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:47,800
I won't abandon you.

138
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,440
Did something happen? I'm very worried.

139
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,520
I'm looking for you near your house.

140
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:00,640
The number you called cannot be connected.

141
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,400
Please try again later.

142
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:06,400
What now? You're not picking up!

143
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:26,880
Hey, Miss!

144
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,200
Are you talking to me?

145
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,720
You're the girl!

146
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:32,640
Sorry, I don't know you.

147
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:36,240
Are you looking for a good looking
young man with fair skin?

148
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,120
Yes!

149
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:38,880
He went over there looking for you!

150
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,480
Thank you, uncle!

151
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:44,320
Hurry! Before someone grabs
a good catch like him.

152
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:55,520
YY!

153
00:09:55,680 --> 00:09:57,440
(Sweet dreams)

154
00:09:57,520 --> 00:10:02,400
(is what he said as he went underground)

155
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:03,360
Over there!

156
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:06,000
(away from me into the dark)

157
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:08,640
(Forced me)

158
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:16,640
(from all my innocence into the very
ordinary day today)

159
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:26,480
(Watch and wait and see what comes)

160
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:32,560
(from the soul of the man who is uncertain)

161
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:38,160
(When the sand washes out to the sea)

162
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:38,960
I can finally see you again.

163
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,640
(when the dreams fall away)

164
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:43,760
I'm so worried...so worried about you.

165
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:47,600
(will there still be someone
there for me...)

166
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:50,240
I was afraid you'd leave without
saying goodbye!

167
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:52,320
(for me)

168
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:55,360
Don't be silly! Why would I do that?

169
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:01,920
You're holding me so tight I can't breathe.

170
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:04,320
(He sings and)

171
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,680
I'm not letting go.

172
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:07,920
(with his hands he holds a microphone)

173
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:08,560
Childish!

174
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:12,400
(and speaks so loud for all to hear)

175
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:13,360
(I'd give)

176
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,680
Why didn't you pick up the phone?

177
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:18,760
(whatever is left of all the work I'd do)

178
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:20,160
The battery died because you kept calling.

179
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:22,800
(my hands are tired from all the years)

180
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:36,240
Did the Police arrest Ken?

181
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:40,880
The creep denied killing Emma!

182
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:44,480
He won't even admit he was Emma's boyfriend.

183
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:45,800
No way!

184
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:47,360
When I looked for him at HKIU,

185
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:49,040
he admitted it

186
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,280
and conned me into following him
to the studio.

187
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:53,760
If he denied it, you wouldn't follow him.

188
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:55,440
Then he couldn't blackmail your father.

189
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,200
You're right.

190
00:11:57,360 --> 00:12:00,080
No wonder in the CCTV footage,

191
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:02,320
he practically ignored Emma.

192
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,800
Ken also told Kwan Sir

193
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:10,800
Emma's boyfriend is someone called James.

194
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:14,320
Who's James?

195
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,080
Ken said James is also from Hong Kong

196
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,920
but emigrated to the UK many years ago.

197
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:20,240
A year ago, he was at HKIU on an
exchange program

198
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:21,520
and he met Ken.

199
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:24,160
Ken took him to the bar where he met Emma.

200
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:25,520
They started dating.

201
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:27,440
But three months ago,
the exchange program ended,

202
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:30,240
and they maintained a
long distance relationship.

203
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:32,240
Ken said James knew he had the connections

204
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:35,520
so James asked him to help smuggle
Emma to the UK.

205
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:40,320
Emma said her dream was to
venture out into this world.

206
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:44,000
I only know if I don't leave,

207
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:46,160
I'll regret it in the future.

208
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:49,440
So her boyfriend is in the UK.

209
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,600
No wonder she wanted to run away.

210
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:55,600
She was so close to getting
her dream come true.

211
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:59,120
Kwan Sir said near Meow Lung Kee,
a regular customer at the nearby store,

212
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:01,280
told him on the night of the 8th,

213
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:03,120
a man wearing a dark green windbreaker

214
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:06,080
chased a girl who might be Emma.

215
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:12,240
Look, James has a similar windbreaker.

216
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:15,600
You mean James is in Hong Kong?

217
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,120
Very likely.

218
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:19,360
Kwan Sir already contacted Immigration,

219
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:22,080
to see if he entered Hong Kong recently.

220
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:24,640
If he did, he's a prime suspect.

221
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:27,680
Emma told me she's crazy about
her boyfriend.

222
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:30,000
If they're in love,

223
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:32,320
why would James kill Emma?

224
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:34,000
According to Ken,

225
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:36,920
Emma wanted to go to the UK.

226
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:38,800
James wasn't so keen.

227
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:40,640
What does that mean?

228
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:43,840
James wrote in here he's in Law School.

229
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:45,920
If Emma smuggled into the UK

230
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:48,080
he'll be assisting an illegal alien.

231
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,360
If anyone should find out,

232
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,720
he can't be a lawyer.

233
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:53,120
But that's no reason to kill someone.

234
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:58,480
Another possibility is money.

235
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:00,320
Emma was carrying so much money.

236
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:03,200
He got greedy and had to silence her.

237
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:07,680
Emma ran away from home because of him.

238
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:10,080
How could he do this?

239
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:12,320
It's just my guess.

240
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:17,120
I'll send a post asking for anyone
with dash cam footage of Emma

241
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:19,120
after she left the guesthouse

242
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,800
and see why she didn't get on the boat.

243
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:24,320
I think...we need to start from scratch.

244
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:31,920
But I may not be able to go with you.

245
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,560
You're leaving so soon?

246
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:39,520
Tomorrow night.

247
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:42,160
How are you leaving?

248
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:45,280
I don't know. Daddy made the arrangements.

249
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,360
It'll be dangerous.

250
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:51,200
Why don't we talk to your father

251
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:53,120
and see if there are other options?

252
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,920
No. He saw you dropping me off yesterday.

253
00:14:56,040 --> 00:14:58,240
He got so angry he locked me in my room.

254
00:14:58,400 --> 00:14:59,920
Luckily, Mom let me out

255
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:01,680
so I could come see you.

256
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:11,200
Can you stay?

257
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:12,960
I wish.

258
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:16,320
But I promised Mom I'll go home.

259
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:19,920
I'm worried about your safety.

260
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:23,600
I'm afraid I won't see you again.

261
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:26,160
No.

262
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:30,800
Daddy is very careful,

263
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:32,880
everything should be all set.

264
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:35,040
Don't be so worried.

265
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:37,760
Mom said once we settle down,

266
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:39,200
you can join us over there.

267
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:41,680
They won't keep us apart anymore.

268
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:48,560
What is this?

269
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:50,800
You left it outside the bar.

270
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,320
An avocado?

271
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:57,920
So it fell out of the bag

272
00:15:58,080 --> 00:16:00,080
and you found it?

273
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:04,000
Can you grow avocado like that?

274
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:05,840
It's my first time.

275
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:08,080
It says online it's very hard.

276
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:11,840
But since you dropped it, I'll do my best.

277
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:14,960
I'll keep trying

278
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:19,200
until it can germinate and bear fruit.

279
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:37,280
Kwan Sir tracked James down.

280
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:39,680
He landed in Hong Kong in the afternoon
on the 9th.

281
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:41,520
He's still here.

282
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:44,560
We tracked Emma till the 8th

283
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:45,800
and we lost track of her.

284
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,520
Her time of death was between
the 8th and the 10th.

285
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:50,800
James was probably the last person she saw.

286
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:52,280
Where is James now?

287
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:54,480
When he filled out his landing card,

288
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:56,840
he put down Hotel Cozy.

289
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,440
Kwan Sir already sent someone there.

290
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:00,360
I don't want to wait around.

291
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:03,120
There's still time, let's check it out.

292
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:09,080
Mrs. Sit, the baby is fine.

293
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,400
Thanks. Dr. Hong!

294
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:12,280
Since you past your first trimester,

295
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:14,880
we can use medication for your vaginitis.

296
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,280
I'll prescribe something
and you must finish the course.

297
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:21,760
I'm taking three weeks off.

298
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,320
I went over your case with Dr. Lam

299
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:27,520
who will keep me posted of your situation.

300
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:29,120
You have nothing to worry about.

301
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:30,720
Dr. Hong, you're so accountable,

302
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:32,320
I'm not worried at all.

303
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:34,040
Sorry! Let me get that.

304
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:35,840
Hello? Yes.

305
00:17:36,040 --> 00:17:41,040
The uterine polypectomy for Mrs. Ng

306
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:44,040
was passed to Dr. Ma, yes...

307
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,960
Mrs. Sit! Let's go fill your prescription.

308
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:50,160
OK!

309
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:54,080
Dr. Hong, you're busier on leave
than when you're at work.

310
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:55,560
Give me the file.

311
00:17:56,440 --> 00:18:02,240
Oh dear! Mrs. Sit is allergic to this drug.

312
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:03,920
I prescribed the wrong drug. Go stop her!

313
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,200
Hurry!
OK!

314
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,800
Elsa, where are you?

315
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:16,880
What time will you be home?

316
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:20,240
You're home!

317
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:23,440
Yes.

318
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:27,920
Just now I prescribed the wrong
drug for a patient.

319
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,880
Luckily I caught it in time,

320
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:31,600
or the result would be unthinkable.

321
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:33,760
You have too much on your mind.

322
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:35,680
Don't blame yourself.

323
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:40,040
Where's Elsa? Is she packed?

324
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:42,280
She...was up all night.

325
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,400
Let her sleep a bit longer.

326
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:48,080
What's in the box?

327
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:51,200
Hospital documents and bank letters.

328
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:52,400
I'll go shred them.

329
00:18:57,520 --> 00:19:01,280
Elsa, where are you? Daddy is home.

330
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:18,880
Where's Elsa's phone?

331
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:24,960
Where's Elsa? Is she packed?

332
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:26,960
She...was up all night.

333
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,360
She's sound asleep right now.

334
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:30,280
Let her sleep a bit longer.

335
00:19:34,520 --> 00:19:36,880
Felix, since we're leaving,

336
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:40,040
I guess we won't be coming back.

337
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:42,280
Can you take a walk with me?

338
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:44,240
The hospital just called.

339
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:47,120
Something urgent came up and they want me
to handle it.

340
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:49,440
I'll do that when I get back, OK?

341
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:08,360
Did Felix find out I let Elsa out?

342
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:11,120
I think it's odd.

343
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:12,800
If James was the killer,

344
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,480
why is he still here?

345
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,400
We'll know when we find him.

346
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:18,480
I'll go find out.

347
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:23,120
Excuse me, I'm looking for your guest
Chan Lap-jim.

348
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:26,560
Sorry, we can't disclose our
guest's privacy.

349
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:29,920
Why didn't you call back?

350
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:32,880
I think Daddy realized I let you out.

351
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,520
He went out to look for you.

352
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:37,560
Oh dear! I missed Mom's message.

353
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,120
Daddy must be looking for me everywhere.

354
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,120
You were meeting your friend in our cafe,

355
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,280
but he didn't show up.

356
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:45,440
You're worried he passed out in his room?

357
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:48,160
He has a health condition, I'm worried.

358
00:20:48,360 --> 00:20:50,160
All I can say is you don't have to worry.

359
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:51,800
He went out?

360
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,600
I see.

361
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:55,840
Do you know where he went?

362
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,360
He just came to Hong Kong,

363
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:58,640
he doesn't know his way around.

364
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:01,600
Well...most people ask us about
scenic spots.

365
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:04,560
But someone asked me the way to
Wan Sing Industrial Building yesterday.

366
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:07,120
Thanks. Wan Sing Industrial Building.

367
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,400
Thank you...

368
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:11,640
Wan Sing Industrial Building...

369
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:14,720
Your family called?

370
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:18,400
Yes. She said Daddy knew I went out.

371
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:20,080
You should hurry home.

372
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,360
I'll keep looking.

373
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:25,280
No. Whether I go home now or later,
I'll get a scolding from Daddy anyway.

374
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:27,520
I'd rather go with you to find James.

375
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:30,000
I want to meet Emma's boyfriend.

376
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:31,520
Let's hurry.

377
00:21:32,080 --> 00:21:35,120
You think we should tell Kwan Sir

378
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:37,360
what we found out about James?

379
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:39,080
We don't know what he's doing there

380
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:40,520
or if he's even there at all.

381
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:42,040
Let's wait till we find out more.

382
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,120
Come on.

383
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:48,600
Well? Did you find Chan Lap-jim?

384
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:50,160
Nothing.

385
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:53,200
James checked into Room 701 of Hotel Cozy.

386
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:55,520
But according to the room card record,

387
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,160
he hasn't been back since last night.

388
00:21:57,240 --> 00:22:00,040
He's on the run? He's hiding something.

389
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:02,400
Anything on the human trafficking cartel?

390
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:04,720
What we found out so far checked out.

391
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:06,480
Ching Sir spoke to the Narcotics Bureau (NB)

392
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:08,720
they're following up on a
human trafficking cartel

393
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:10,560
that is also involved in drug trafficking.

394
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:12,560
They'll let us know once they hear anything.

395
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:13,320
Good.

396
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:16,160
I heard the snakehead Brother Man is mean.

397
00:22:16,320 --> 00:22:18,320
I can't believe they're into drugs as well.

398
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:21,640
If he knew Hong Ka-lam had
that much money,

399
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:23,440
he's likely to kill her.

400
00:22:23,560 --> 00:22:24,720
Other than Chan Lap-jim,

401
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:27,360
these guys are likely the last people
to see Hong Ka-lam alive.

402
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:29,640
We must find them soon.

403
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:33,600
Hello? Yes...where?

404
00:22:33,760 --> 00:22:35,320
OK, thanks!

405
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:36,880
They found their hideout.

406
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:38,240
In Wan Sing Industrial Building.

407
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:40,040
Once NB gets the search warrant,

408
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:40,960
we can bust them.

409
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:58,640
I wonder where James is.

410
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:01,080
We need to check all these units
one by one?

411
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:03,040
Why did he come here?

412
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:09,560
It's Daddy! Over there...

413
00:23:15,760 --> 00:23:16,840
It's really him!

414
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,160
What is he doing here?

415
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,720
How many times have you been to a bar?

416
00:23:20,800 --> 00:23:23,360
When did you set a tracker on my phone?

417
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:24,720
That's outrageous!

418
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:29,040
Daddy put in a GPS tracker on Emma's phone.

419
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:30,480
Maybe he did the same to mine.

420
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:33,640
Shall I turn off the phone?

421
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:35,640
Yes, but not now.

422
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:42,840
This way.

423
00:23:43,240 --> 00:23:44,120
Where are we going?

424
00:23:44,280 --> 00:23:45,120
Somewhere far away.

425
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:54,880
Will Daddy find us?

426
00:23:55,080 --> 00:23:56,160
Trust me.

427
00:24:12,680 --> 00:24:13,600
Let's go.

428
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:20,360
There's no signal?!

429
00:24:21,040 --> 00:24:22,960
Maybe reception is poor on her phone.

430
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:24,840
She can't be too far away.

431
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:33,200
Your father probably won't expect
us to come back.

432
00:24:33,360 --> 00:24:35,120
You're so brilliant! What now?

433
00:24:35,280 --> 00:24:37,640
Wai, don't you look smart in that jacket!

434
00:24:37,760 --> 00:24:40,160
You think so? It's a bit too big.

435
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:41,320
Not really.

436
00:24:41,640 --> 00:24:44,520
That looks like the one James has.

437
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:45,640
Follow him.

438
00:24:48,960 --> 00:24:50,400
Wait up...

439
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:31,200
Stop! I told you I'm not a cop.

440
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:37,560
The cops busted my hideout in
Meow Lung Kee.

441
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:41,120
If you're not a cop, how did you find us?

442
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:43,120
I don't know about any raids.

443
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:46,400
I'm looking for my girlfriend Hong Ka-lam.

444
00:25:48,360 --> 00:25:50,160
Why is he looking for Emma here?

445
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:52,920
It doesn't sound like he killed her.

446
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:56,120
You're making this up to get away.

447
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:58,280
I'm not lying.

448
00:25:58,360 --> 00:26:00,720
Ken told me I can find you here.

449
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:03,360
Ken who? You're making it up...

450
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:07,280
Call the Police!

451
00:26:11,280 --> 00:26:14,000
Boss, those two are snooping around.

452
00:26:14,080 --> 00:26:15,920
The dude is calling someone.

453
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:18,320
Who are you?

454
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:19,320
Wrong floor.

455
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:20,280
Stop!

456
00:26:20,400 --> 00:26:20,960
Come back!

457
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:21,600
Go!

458
00:26:21,720 --> 00:26:22,600
Hey...

459
00:26:22,680 --> 00:26:23,600
Help...

460
00:26:23,760 --> 00:26:24,480
Help...

461
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:25,440
Come back here...

462
00:26:25,600 --> 00:26:26,760
Help...

463
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:28,800
No...

464
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:32,480
Run...

465
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:34,160
Get him!

466
00:26:36,360 --> 00:26:38,280
No...

467
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:41,800
No...

468
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:46,600
Take him inside.

469
00:26:46,760 --> 00:26:47,680
Move!

470
00:26:52,040 --> 00:26:53,440
Boss, we've got them.

471
00:26:53,480 --> 00:26:54,520
What should we do with these two?

472
00:26:54,600 --> 00:26:56,240
What now? Are they cops?

473
00:26:57,160 --> 00:27:00,120
Don't be stupid! Do they look like cops?

474
00:27:00,200 --> 00:27:02,120
But they heard what we said.

475
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:03,360
Lock them up for now.

476
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:04,480
Move!

477
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:09,440
Get down!

478
00:27:10,640 --> 00:27:11,640
You too.

479
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:14,840
No games!

480
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:19,200
Are you hurt?

481
00:27:19,360 --> 00:27:20,880
No. And you?

482
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:21,760
I'm fine.

483
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:24,040
Who are you?

484
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:29,320
James, right? We've been looking for you.

485
00:27:29,440 --> 00:27:30,960
You know me?

486
00:27:31,080 --> 00:27:34,000
I'm Emma's sister, Hong Ka-yee, Elsa.

487
00:27:34,120 --> 00:27:35,800
I know you're Emma's boyfriend.

488
00:27:35,920 --> 00:27:37,120
We've been looking for you.

489
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:38,640
You're Emma's sister?

490
00:27:38,760 --> 00:27:40,240
I know Emma has a sister,

491
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:43,320
but she never told me your name.

492
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:45,680
Where is Emma?

493
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:47,360
She was supposed meet me in the UK.

494
00:27:47,560 --> 00:27:49,800
She contacted me before she boarded the boat

495
00:27:49,920 --> 00:27:52,320
but I don't know if she has
got on it or not.

496
00:27:52,440 --> 00:27:54,000
I was so worried

497
00:27:54,120 --> 00:27:56,120
I came here right away to look for her.

498
00:27:56,600 --> 00:27:57,880
What are you doing here?

499
00:27:58,000 --> 00:27:59,680
Did Ken tell you about this place?

500
00:27:59,760 --> 00:28:01,920
Ken is such a jerk.

501
00:28:02,080 --> 00:28:04,520
I entrusted him with helping Emma
skip town.

502
00:28:04,640 --> 00:28:06,560
Not only did he try to rob her,

503
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:08,160
he also wounded her.

504
00:28:08,320 --> 00:28:10,520
I've been trying to find him
since I arrived

505
00:28:10,640 --> 00:28:12,640
and he's been dodging me.

506
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:16,080
Luckily I asked him about the
human trafficking cartel before.

507
00:28:16,240 --> 00:28:18,160
That's why I know this place.

508
00:28:18,360 --> 00:28:21,200
Where is Emma?

509
00:28:25,480 --> 00:28:27,920
Emma is dead.

510
00:28:28,200 --> 00:28:31,600
She was the faceless corpse in the news.

511
00:28:32,160 --> 00:28:36,400
What? Emma is dead?

512
00:28:36,760 --> 00:28:39,760
How? And why?

513
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:41,360
That's what we want to know.

514
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:42,960
The Police is looking for the killer.

515
00:28:43,440 --> 00:28:45,080
Who killed her?

516
00:28:45,240 --> 00:28:46,880
We thought it was Ken at first.

517
00:28:47,040 --> 00:28:50,080
But he only admitted to wounding
and robbing her.

518
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:51,600
He denied killing her.

519
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:53,600
I don't think it was him.

520
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:56,240
Emma spoke to me on the phone
before she boarded the boat

521
00:28:56,360 --> 00:28:58,080
and told me she was almost at the pier.

522
00:28:58,200 --> 00:29:00,240
I didn't think Ken caught up with her.

523
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:01,680
But a witness said

524
00:29:01,800 --> 00:29:03,640
near the hillside where they found Emma

525
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:05,880
he saw a tall man chasing Emma.

526
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:08,160
He was wearing a dark green windbreaker.

527
00:29:08,320 --> 00:29:09,680
I saw on Instabook,

528
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:11,760
you had the exact same windbreaker.

529
00:29:11,920 --> 00:29:14,040
You think I killed Emma?

530
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:17,760
I love her. Why would I kill her?

531
00:29:17,920 --> 00:29:20,080
Ken said he could sense that

532
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:22,400
you didn't want Emma to go to the UK.

533
00:29:22,520 --> 00:29:23,600
Is that so?

534
00:29:24,720 --> 00:29:27,800
It's not what you think...

535
00:29:28,120 --> 00:29:30,120
Emma told me before

536
00:29:30,280 --> 00:29:33,040
your father found out you guys
went to a bar

537
00:29:33,200 --> 00:29:35,440
and he was likely to confiscate your phones.

538
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:37,760
If I couldn't get in touch with her

539
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:39,440
I need not worry about her.

540
00:29:42,320 --> 00:29:46,480
(Day 1 after Emma left)

541
00:29:50,960 --> 00:29:53,680
I finally get to see you. Are you OK?

542
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:55,520
Why are you in a taxi?

543
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:57,200
I ran away from home.

544
00:29:57,360 --> 00:29:59,840
I have made up my mind.
I'm not going back.

545
00:29:59,960 --> 00:30:02,120
Where can you go if you don't go back?

546
00:30:02,280 --> 00:30:05,520
I'll come to you. I want to be with you.

547
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:06,960
Ken has the connections,

548
00:30:07,120 --> 00:30:08,840
he'll find a way to help us.

549
00:30:08,960 --> 00:30:10,160
You're being impulsive.

550
00:30:10,360 --> 00:30:12,240
You left home without a plan.

551
00:30:12,400 --> 00:30:14,400
I've been locked up for three weeks.

552
00:30:14,560 --> 00:30:16,160
I planned everything.

553
00:30:16,320 --> 00:30:18,880
Just tell Ken to contact people

554
00:30:19,080 --> 00:30:20,640
who can send me to you.

555
00:30:20,800 --> 00:30:22,960
I also took money from Daddy's safe.

556
00:30:23,120 --> 00:30:25,200
We can finally be together.

557
00:30:25,320 --> 00:30:26,520
Don't you want that?

558
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:29,560
OK...I'll get Ken to help you.

559
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:30,600
Bye!

560
00:30:36,640 --> 00:30:39,200
(Day 3 after Emma left)

561
00:30:44,160 --> 00:30:45,440
Why are you bleeding?

562
00:30:45,600 --> 00:30:47,680
Ken tried to rob me!

563
00:30:47,760 --> 00:30:49,440
Luckily I got most of it back.

564
00:30:49,600 --> 00:30:52,120
Since it was getting late,

565
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:54,520
I told her to hurry over to Meow Lung Kee.

566
00:30:54,640 --> 00:30:56,640
Because she can't miss the boat.

567
00:30:58,360 --> 00:31:00,160
(Ngan Kai Bay Pier)

568
00:31:02,120 --> 00:31:04,640
Meow Lung Kee is the code name
for Ngan Kai Bay Pier.

569
00:31:04,720 --> 00:31:06,880
Follow this path for ten minutes,

570
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:08,080
you'll see a steep road

571
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:09,360
and the pier is right there.

572
00:31:09,560 --> 00:31:10,880
It's so complicated.

573
00:31:11,040 --> 00:31:13,880
It's dark and I'm scared.

574
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:15,640
Just keep going.

575
00:31:15,760 --> 00:31:17,120
Judging from your current location,

576
00:31:17,320 --> 00:31:18,760
you're not far from the pier.

577
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:21,680
Once you get on the boat, I'll see you soon.

578
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:25,280
You're breaking up, reception is poor.

579
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:27,880
Call me after you land.

580
00:31:28,040 --> 00:31:29,440
I'll come get you right away.

581
00:31:29,600 --> 00:31:30,720
OK, bye!

582
00:31:31,080 --> 00:31:34,560
I lost track of her after that.

583
00:31:34,680 --> 00:31:37,880
I was worried and I thought...

584
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:40,840
maybe there was no signal on the boat.

585
00:31:40,960 --> 00:31:42,800
But not long after that,

586
00:31:42,960 --> 00:31:44,640
she sent me a message

587
00:31:44,800 --> 00:31:47,320
telling me she'd rather stay in Hong Kong.

588
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:49,360
I thought that was odd.

589
00:31:49,480 --> 00:31:51,800
Why did she change her mind so suddenly?

590
00:31:51,920 --> 00:31:54,040
No matter how many messages I sent her,

591
00:31:54,200 --> 00:31:55,880
she never texted back.

592
00:31:56,120 --> 00:31:57,520
I became very worried

593
00:31:57,680 --> 00:31:59,560
and caught the next flight to Hong Kong.

594
00:31:59,920 --> 00:32:03,800
After I landed, I still couldn't
get in touch with her.

595
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,080
Emma was very protective of her family.

596
00:32:06,240 --> 00:32:09,800
She never told me where she lived.

597
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:13,280
Then I thought the snakehead should know

598
00:32:13,400 --> 00:32:16,120
what happened to Emma on the boat
on that night.

599
00:32:16,280 --> 00:32:19,280
I asked Ken about the
human trafficking cartel.

600
00:32:19,440 --> 00:32:23,640
But he only told me the name of
an industrial building.

601
00:32:23,760 --> 00:32:26,760
But I didn't get the name right.

602
00:32:26,920 --> 00:32:30,040
I only remember Wan something
Industrial Building.

603
00:32:30,160 --> 00:32:34,360
It took me a long time to find
my way here.

604
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:35,920
When I finally came here...

605
00:32:36,080 --> 00:32:37,080
Who are you?

606
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:39,360
I asked them if they have seen
Emma on the 8th.

607
00:32:39,520 --> 00:32:41,520
They pulled me inside

608
00:32:41,640 --> 00:32:43,440
and asked me how I found them.

609
00:32:43,600 --> 00:32:45,320
I told them Ken told me.

610
00:32:45,440 --> 00:32:47,840
We heard you from outside.

611
00:32:47,960 --> 00:32:50,880
But they didn't seem to know Ken.

612
00:32:51,080 --> 00:32:54,040
Maybe Ken went through someone else.

613
00:32:54,160 --> 00:33:00,000
I didn't find out anything
and got beaten up.

614
00:33:00,200 --> 00:33:03,160
Trust me. I only wanted to find Emma.

615
00:33:03,240 --> 00:33:04,280
I didn't kill her.

616
00:33:14,760 --> 00:33:17,920
Trust me. I only wanted to find Emma.

617
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:19,320
I didn't kill her.

618
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:21,040
I believe you.

619
00:33:21,160 --> 00:33:23,360
If you killed her,
you should have left town.

620
00:33:23,440 --> 00:33:26,160
Why would you be here?

621
00:33:26,280 --> 00:33:28,880
Why didn't I come back sooner?

622
00:33:28,960 --> 00:33:33,200
Why did I let her board the boat by herself?

623
00:33:33,280 --> 00:33:36,240
I thought Ken was right about you

624
00:33:36,320 --> 00:33:38,840
and you didn't want Emma to find you
in the UK.

625
00:33:38,960 --> 00:33:41,360
If Emma smuggled into the UK,

626
00:33:41,480 --> 00:33:43,760
you probably can't be a lawyer.

627
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:46,680
Yes, I hesitated.

628
00:33:47,040 --> 00:33:48,560
I thought I could wait till I finish school

629
00:33:48,640 --> 00:33:51,640
and come back to Hong Kong to be with her.

630
00:33:51,760 --> 00:33:53,160
But I knew at that moment,

631
00:33:53,320 --> 00:33:55,320
Emma didn't want to stay at home anymore.

632
00:33:55,640 --> 00:33:59,360
She had no one else but me.

633
00:33:59,520 --> 00:34:02,560
I made up my mind

634
00:34:02,720 --> 00:34:04,960
I'll give up being a lawyer.

635
00:34:05,120 --> 00:34:08,560
I already applied with the university
to change my major.

636
00:34:08,720 --> 00:34:10,760
After she arrived in the UK,

637
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:12,880
we'll keep a low profile

638
00:34:13,040 --> 00:34:16,240
and live a simple life.

639
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:21,520
But now, it won't happen...

640
00:34:22,840 --> 00:34:27,600
Emma should be very touched
to hear you say this.

641
00:34:28,800 --> 00:34:31,040
I'm sure she heard me.

642
00:34:32,360 --> 00:34:34,320
Let's try to get out of here.

643
00:34:40,600 --> 00:34:41,760
What are you doing?

644
00:34:41,960 --> 00:34:43,840
Sit down!

645
00:34:45,200 --> 00:34:47,920
You overheard everything.

646
00:34:48,080 --> 00:34:49,840
I'll give each of you a shot

647
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:51,520
and then throw you in the water.

648
00:34:51,640 --> 00:34:52,400
Do it!

649
00:34:52,560 --> 00:34:53,600
Yes, Boss!

650
00:34:55,880 --> 00:34:56,800
You first!

651
00:34:56,840 --> 00:35:00,160
No...
Don't move!

652
00:35:00,440 --> 00:35:01,760
You...

653
00:35:02,760 --> 00:35:04,000
You hit me?

654
00:35:04,120 --> 00:35:05,520
Boss, cops are outside!

655
00:35:05,640 --> 00:35:07,360
Clear out!
Run...

656
00:35:08,360 --> 00:35:10,480
Run...

657
00:35:11,640 --> 00:35:12,480
Police! Freeze!

658
00:35:12,760 --> 00:35:14,480
Police! Nobody moves! Raise your hands!

659
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:18,400
Police! Stay where you are!

660
00:35:18,520 --> 00:35:21,840
Police! Freeze!
Get down!

661
00:35:22,120 --> 00:35:28,680
Don't resist!
Run...

662
00:35:28,840 --> 00:35:32,240
Don't move...
Get down...

663
00:35:39,160 --> 00:35:41,840
You should go. I'll call you.

664
00:35:41,960 --> 00:35:43,520
I'm leaving tomorrow night.

665
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:53,640
I'll call you tonight.

666
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:06,640
Kwan Sir!

667
00:36:06,720 --> 00:36:09,240
YY...what are you doing here?

668
00:36:09,400 --> 00:36:12,320
Long story. I'll go with you
and give you a statement.

669
00:36:12,440 --> 00:36:13,440
Let's go...

670
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:17,360
You're late!

671
00:36:17,520 --> 00:36:18,720
Where's Daddy?

672
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:32,400
Felix, tonight is our last night
in this house.

673
00:36:32,560 --> 00:36:38,720
Let's just enjoy our last dinner, OK?

674
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:41,680
OK, let's eat.

675
00:36:42,320 --> 00:36:43,520
OK?

676
00:36:58,640 --> 00:37:01,840
I made a mistake today.

677
00:37:03,520 --> 00:37:07,760
I prescribed the wrong drug to a patient.

678
00:37:08,160 --> 00:37:10,320
Everyone makes mistakes.

679
00:37:10,440 --> 00:37:12,080
Don't blame yourself.

680
00:37:12,200 --> 00:37:15,120
But...I'm a doctor.

681
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:17,160
I cannot make mistakes.

682
00:37:17,640 --> 00:37:22,720
Because some mistakes are irreversible.

683
00:37:26,520 --> 00:37:28,880
Elsa...

684
00:37:29,200 --> 00:37:31,440
your sister ran away from home

685
00:37:31,560 --> 00:37:33,280
and it was my mistake.

686
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:36,240
I already lost your sister,

687
00:37:36,480 --> 00:37:39,280
I can't lose you too.

688
00:37:39,640 --> 00:37:42,240
That's why I'm so hard on you,

689
00:37:42,520 --> 00:37:44,960
Do you understand?

690
00:37:50,680 --> 00:37:53,160
I do.

691
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:08,400
After we leave here, we can start over.

692
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:24,400
Hello, YY?

693
00:38:24,520 --> 00:38:26,880
Elsa, is everything OK at home?

694
00:38:27,040 --> 00:38:29,920
They didn't scold me.

695
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:31,920
It was actually my fault.

696
00:38:32,040 --> 00:38:35,520
I snuck out and made Daddy worried.

697
00:38:35,640 --> 00:38:37,240
That's why he followed me.

698
00:38:37,360 --> 00:38:39,920
Did you give your statement?

699
00:38:40,120 --> 00:38:41,520
Kwan Sir asked me who you are.

700
00:38:41,560 --> 00:38:42,880
I told him I don't know you.

701
00:38:43,040 --> 00:38:44,960
I don't think he believed me.

702
00:38:45,120 --> 00:38:46,400
But he can't do anything to me.

703
00:38:46,560 --> 00:38:49,520
Good. I was worried about
getting you involved.

704
00:38:49,640 --> 00:38:52,840
I'm calling you about something
very important.

705
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:54,680
Promise me you'll stay calm.

706
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:03,120
Shall we take this with us?

707
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:05,440
Sure!

708
00:39:33,720 --> 00:39:34,960
Phone?

709
00:39:35,160 --> 00:39:36,960
Yes, I'm going tonight.

710
00:39:37,120 --> 00:39:38,720
Why do you have two phones?

711
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:48,120
This is my new chat app.

712
00:39:48,240 --> 00:39:49,760
I'll contact you on my new phone.

713
00:39:49,840 --> 00:39:51,440
Remember this icon.

714
00:39:51,600 --> 00:39:54,240
Daddy is hiding Emma's phone.

715
00:39:54,440 --> 00:39:57,760
I'm calling you about something
very important.

716
00:39:57,920 --> 00:39:59,280
Promise me you'll stay calm.

717
00:39:59,520 --> 00:40:02,200
What is it? You sound serious.

718
00:40:02,360 --> 00:40:03,720
Remember I told you this morning,

719
00:40:03,800 --> 00:40:06,400
I'll send a post to ask for
any dash cam footage of Emma

720
00:40:06,520 --> 00:40:08,560
after she left the guesthouse.

721
00:40:08,680 --> 00:40:09,720
I remember.

722
00:40:09,920 --> 00:40:11,640
I just received a clip,

723
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:16,200
between 4 and 5 o'clock
near the guesthouse.

724
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:17,120
I'm sending it to you now.

725
00:40:17,200 --> 00:40:18,080
(Share with Elsa?)

726
00:40:18,160 --> 00:40:19,200
OK!

727
00:40:19,880 --> 00:40:21,640
He was chasing your sister.

728
00:40:21,720 --> 00:40:24,800
Grabbed her and tried to take her somewhere.

729
00:40:24,880 --> 00:40:26,080
but your sister got away.

730
00:40:26,120 --> 00:40:27,520
That was Daddy.

731
00:40:27,640 --> 00:40:30,320
He saw her on the 8th.

732
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:32,320
Why did he lie?

733
00:40:32,440 --> 00:40:34,880
He said he went out every day
but didn't find Emma.

734
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:39,120
Wait...look at the jacket he was wearing.

735
00:40:41,480 --> 00:40:45,680
It looks so much like James'.

736
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:48,680
The customer of the store said
he saw a man chasing a girl,

737
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:51,840
wearing a dark green windbreaker

738
00:40:51,960 --> 00:40:54,080
and was 175cm tall.

739
00:40:54,200 --> 00:40:55,720
Is that your father's height?

740
00:40:55,880 --> 00:40:57,720
You suspect he killed Emma?

741
00:40:57,880 --> 00:41:00,000
No, it's impossible.

742
00:41:00,080 --> 00:41:01,600
Daddy loves us very much.

743
00:41:01,720 --> 00:41:03,520
Even if Emma disobeyed him,

744
00:41:03,680 --> 00:41:05,760
he couldn't have killed her.

745
00:41:05,960 --> 00:41:07,600
Elsa, calm down.

746
00:41:07,720 --> 00:41:10,000
I'm not saying he's the killer.

747
00:41:10,200 --> 00:41:11,600
It's a possibility.

748
00:41:11,720 --> 00:41:14,400
Why else did he lie about seeing Emma?

749
00:41:14,480 --> 00:41:16,480
No, it can't be.

750
00:41:16,560 --> 00:41:18,240
If your father was the killer,

751
00:41:18,360 --> 00:41:20,640
the new phone Emma was using
when she left

752
00:41:20,720 --> 00:41:22,720
should be in his possession.

753
00:41:22,800 --> 00:41:23,920
Try to look for it.

754
00:41:26,600 --> 00:41:29,040
Did Daddy really kill Emma?

755
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:37,640
Hello, YY! I found Emma's new phone.

756
00:41:37,800 --> 00:41:39,280
That means on the 8th,

757
00:41:39,400 --> 00:41:42,120
your father found Emma near
the guesthouse

758
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:45,360
and he followed her
all the way to Meow Lung Kee.

759
00:41:45,520 --> 00:41:48,160
Emma refused to come home with him.

760
00:41:48,240 --> 00:41:52,120
He got so angry...he killed Emma.

761
00:41:52,560 --> 00:41:54,200
Then he took her phone,

762
00:41:54,280 --> 00:41:56,640
posed as Emma and sent a message to James

763
00:41:56,720 --> 00:41:58,800
to break up with him

764
00:41:58,880 --> 00:42:02,800
so James won't suspect
why Emma didn't get on the boat.

765
00:42:02,960 --> 00:42:06,000
When I suspected the corpse was Emma.

766
00:42:06,160 --> 00:42:08,400
He posed as Emma again
and sent me a message to tell me

767
00:42:08,520 --> 00:42:09,520
she was safe.

768
00:42:11,080 --> 00:42:13,600
Just so I will stop looking into it.

769
00:42:13,680 --> 00:42:15,640
Elsa, you're in grave danger.

770
00:42:15,720 --> 00:42:16,960
Don't stay in the house.

771
00:42:17,160 --> 00:42:19,440
Drop everything...

772
00:42:19,640 --> 00:42:21,280
find an excuse and leave.

773
00:42:21,480 --> 00:42:22,560
But...

774
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:27,920
Elsa? Hello?

775
00:42:28,360 --> 00:42:32,880
Hello? Elsa...

776
00:42:35,720 --> 00:42:38,480
Elsa?
